STEP 5 -- static inter-VRF routing (tests G5)                             PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: the guide's own escape hatch -- deliberate, route-by-route communication
  between two VRFs -- must work, and must open only what it names. The unrouted
  control in the same capture is what measures the second half.

  Applied 23:29:02, both accepted with no message:
awplus(config)# ip route vrf red  192.168.48.0/24 vlan48
awplus(config)# ip route vrf blue 192.168.10.0/24 vlan10

  The form accepted here is network + EGRESS VLAN, with no next-hop address. The
  guide's p.17 prose says these routes "must specify both the egress VLAN and next
  hop IP address", while its own worked example on the same page uses the VLAN-only
  form (`ip route vrf red 192.168.20.0/24 vlan10`). The VLAN-only form is what this
  build accepts and what works; the prose overstates the requirement.

awplus# show ip route vrf red
  C       192.168.10.0/24 is directly connected, vlan10
  S       192.168.48.0/24 [1/0] is directly connected, vlan48
awplus# show ip route vrf blue
  S       192.168.10.0/24 [1/0] is directly connected, vlan10
  C       192.168.48.0/24 is directly connected, vlan48
awplus# show running-config | include ip route
  ip route vrf red 192.168.48.0/24 vlan48
  ip route vrf blue 192.168.10.0/24 vlan10
                                           <-- a static route in one VRF whose egress
                                               interface lives in the other, rendered
                                               as "is directly connected, <the other
                                               VRF's vlan>"

  Leg V5-inter-vrf-static.  cap eth3: 32 frames.  cap eth4: 7 frames
    192.168.48.2 (SUBJECT, on eth4) : 5 sent, 5 ARRIVED        (0 in V4, immediately before)
    192.168.48.1 (SUBJECT-2)        : 5 sent, 5 echo replies   (0 in V4)
    203.0.113.9  (CONTROL)          : 5 sent, 0 echo replies
    192.168.10.1 (INSTRUMENT)       : 5 sent, 5 echo replies

  => STEP 5 PASS: G5 confirmed on the wire. Two static inter-VRF routes restore
     crossing from 0/5 to 5/5 in both of the measured directions, and the unrouted
